["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>For ducks and geese the shot is set by federal law. For grouse it is your choice. Get it wrong and you can be fined with a duck in your hand.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The shot rule as a flow: hunting ducks, geese, coots or snipe means non toxic shot only, and no lead shells in your possession in the hunting area. Grouse, ptarmigan and other upland birds: lead is legal, unless a local rule says otherwise.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Which shot is legal?</text>\n<rect x=\"90\" y=\"44\" width=\"220\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What are you hunting?</text>\n<line x1=\"160.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"105.6\" y2=\"113.2\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M100.0 116.0 L105.5 108.9 L109.0 115.9Z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<line x1=\"240.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"294.4\" y2=\"113.2\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M300.0 116.0 L291.0 115.9 L294.5 108.9Z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"118\" width=\"186\" height=\"120\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<text x=\"105.0\" y=\"142.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ducks, geese,</text>\n<text x=\"105.0\" y=\"162.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">coots, snipe</text>\n<text x=\"105.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Non toxic only</text>\n<text x=\"105.0\" y=\"214.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No lead even</text>\n<text x=\"105.0\" y=\"230.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in your pocket</text>\n<rect x=\"206\" y=\"118\" width=\"182\" height=\"120\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"297.0\" y=\"142.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grouse, ptarmigan,</text>\n<text x=\"297.0\" y=\"162.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">quail, pheasant</text>\n<text x=\"297.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lead is legal</text>\n<text x=\"297.0\" y=\"214.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">unless a local</text>\n<text x=\"297.0\" y=\"230.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rule bans it</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022, s. 38.</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"292.0\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Study aid only. The regulations are the law.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ducks, geese, coots, snipe: <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Non toxic shot\">Non toxic shot</button> only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Not even a lead shell in your pocket in the hunting area <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law, word for word</summary><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022, s. 38(1)</div><p>\"A person must not hunt a migratory game bird (a) while having in their possession in the hunting area shot other than non-toxic shot; or (b) using shot other than non-toxic shot.\"</p></aside><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">BC synopsis, page 13</div><p>\"Federal regulations currently identify steel shot, bismuth shot, tungsten-iron shot, tungsten-bronze-iron shot, tin shot, tungsten - matrix shot, and tungsten-polymer shot as the only non-toxic shot permitted for use on waterfowl, coot, and snipe.\"</p></aside><ul><li>Lead is still allowed for band tailed pigeon and doves (99%, s. 38(2), (3)).</li><li>Upland birds (grouse, ptarmigan, quail, partridge, pheasant, turkey): the lead ban does not apply, unless a local restriction near an important wetland (99%, page 13).</li><li>Lead is banned in National Wildlife Areas (95%, <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide\">Ammo for your guns</a>).</li><li>Near you: no lead shot for any purpose on or seaward of any Delta dyke, or the Surrey dykes facing Mud Bay (99%, page 27, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>).</li><li>Full Rule Book screens: <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/32\">federal methods</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/12\">BC shot ban notice</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Shot density in grams per cubic centimetre: steel about 7.8, bismuth about 9.6 to 9.8, lead about 11.2 to 11.3, tungsten super shot about 18. Denser pellets keep more energy, so you can use a smaller size.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">How heavy is each shot?</text>\n<text x=\"20.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Steel</text>\n<rect x=\"150\" y=\"64\" width=\"82\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<text x=\"237.9\" y=\"83.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">7.8</text>\n<text x=\"20.0\" y=\"132.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bismuth</text>\n<rect x=\"150\" y=\"114\" width=\"102\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<text x=\"257.9\" y=\"133.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">9.7</text>\n<text x=\"20.0\" y=\"182.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Lead</text>\n<rect x=\"150\" y=\"164\" width=\"119\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#5d646b\"/>\n<text x=\"274.6\" y=\"183.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">11.3</text>\n<text x=\"20.0\" y=\"232.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tungsten (TSS)</text>\n<rect x=\"150\" y=\"214\" width=\"189\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<text x=\"345.0\" y=\"233.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">18</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"262\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<text x=\"42.0\" y=\"273.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">non toxic: legal for ducks</text>\n<rect x=\"250\" y=\"262\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#5d646b\"/>\n<text x=\"272.0\" y=\"273.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">lead</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"290.0\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">g/cm3, about</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Steel: cheapest, lightest, hard on tight chokes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Bismuth: softer, closer to lead, safer in old guns <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Tungsten (TSS, tungsten super shot): densest, priciest <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: each one in full</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Shot</th><th>Density</th><th>Good</th><th>Watch out</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Steel</td><td>about 7.8 g/cm3</td><td>Cheap, everywhere</td><td>Lighter, loses energy, needs a steel rated choke</td></tr><tr><td>Bismuth</td><td>about 9.6 to 9.8</td><td>Soft like lead, kinder to older guns</td><td>Costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Lead</td><td>about 11.2 to 11.3</td><td>Dense, cheap</td><td>Illegal for ducks and geese</td></tr><tr><td>Tungsten (TSS)</td><td>about 18</td><td>Densest: small pellets hit hard</td><td>Very expensive. Ask your maker first</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Densities: NWTF (National Wild Turkey Federation) and Outdoor Life articles, search previews <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Steel is about 100 times harder than lead and two thirds as dense; it \"may therefore damage chokes on older firearms\" (70%, Wikipedia, shot).</li><li>Bismuth \"is generally safe to use in older shotguns with barrels and chokes not rated for use with steel shot\" (70%, Wikipedia, shot). Ask a gunsmith about an old gun anyway (Tip).</li><li>Tungsten super shot in a gun or choke not rated for it: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with the gun and choke maker before you buy a box.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Shot sizes to scale, diameter in millimetres: No. 7.5 2.4, No. 6 2.8, No. 4 3.3, No. 2 3.8, BB 4.6. Bigger number, smaller pellet.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Shot sizes to scale</text>\n<circle cx=\"46\" cy=\"130\" r=\"14.5\" fill=\"#a7aeb3\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"46.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No. 7.5</text>\n<text x=\"46.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.4 mm</text>\n<text x=\"46.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grouse</text>\n<circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"130\" r=\"16.7\" fill=\"#a7aeb3\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"122.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No. 6</text>\n<text x=\"122.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.8 mm</text>\n<text x=\"122.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grouse</text>\n<circle cx=\"198\" cy=\"130\" r=\"19.8\" fill=\"#a7aeb3\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"198.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No. 4</text>\n<text x=\"198.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3.3 mm</text>\n<text x=\"198.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">teal</text>\n<circle cx=\"274\" cy=\"130\" r=\"22.9\" fill=\"#a7aeb3\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"274.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No. 2</text>\n<text x=\"274.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3.8 mm</text>\n<text x=\"274.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ducks</text>\n<circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"130\" r=\"27.4\" fill=\"#a7aeb3\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"350.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BB</text>\n<text x=\"350.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4.6 mm</text>\n<text x=\"350.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">geese</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"280.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bigger number, smaller pellet.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bigger number, smaller pellet <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Same size, steel is lighter than lead, so go about 2 sizes bigger in steel (Tip, 60%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: sizes in full</summary><ul><li>Diameters: No. 7.5 2.41 mm, No. 6 2.79 mm, No. 4 3.30 mm, No. 2 3.81 mm, BB 4.57 mm (70%, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-mastery/6\">Shotgun mastery</a>, Wikipedia).</li><li>Steel No. 2: about 125 pellets per ounce. Lead No. 6: about 225 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Deer: buckshot No. 1 or bigger, 20 gauge or bigger, where shotguns are legal for deer. Bird shot never (95 to 99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/8\">Rule Book</a>). This course is about birds.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How to read a shell box: 1 gauge, 2 shell length, 3 shot material, 4 shot size, 5 shot weight in ounces, 6 speed in feet per second.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Read the box</text>\n<rect x=\"30\" y=\"50\" width=\"340\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<text x=\"92.0\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 GA</text>\n<circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"74\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"79.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 in</text>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"74\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"79.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<text x=\"308.0\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">STEEL</text>\n<circle cx=\"308\" cy=\"74\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"308\" y=\"79.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n<text x=\"92.0\" y=\"180.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No. 2</text>\n<circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"148\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"153.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"180.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 1/4 oz</text>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"148\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"153.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text>\n<text x=\"308.0\" y=\"180.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1450 fps</text>\n<circle cx=\"308\" cy=\"148\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"308\" y=\"153.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text>\n<text x=\"40.0\" y=\"228.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">1 gauge</text>\n<text x=\"160.0\" y=\"228.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">2 length</text>\n<text x=\"280.0\" y=\"228.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 material</text>\n<text x=\"40.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 size</text>\n<text x=\"160.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">5 weight</text>\n<text x=\"280.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">6 speed</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"290.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Example box. Check every line.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Gauge, length, material, size, weight, speed <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Gauge and length must match your barrel (<a href=\"#/s/mc-shotgun-05\">Chapter 5</a>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the lines on a box</summary><ul><li>Weight is the shot load in ounces or grams. Speed is in feet per second (fps) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Beretta's A300 manual warns against European \"High Performance\" (HP) steel loads with pellets over 3.5 mm in that gun (95%, 09/2011 manual). Whether North American steel BB counts: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with Beretta Canada before you buy goose loads for an A300.</li><li>Use only factory loaded shells: Beretta and Stoeger void the warranty for reloads <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Starting shells by bird: teal steel No. 4; mallard and wigeon steel No. 2 or 3; Canada goose steel BB; ruffed grouse lead No. 7.5 or 6; bismuth or tungsten work for all of them at a higher price.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Starting shells by bird</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"46\" width=\"376\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"24.0\" y=\"72.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Teal</text>\n<text x=\"376.0\" y=\"72.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"end\">Steel No. 4</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"92\" width=\"376\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"24.0\" y=\"118.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mallard, wigeon</text>\n<text x=\"376.0\" y=\"118.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"end\">Steel No. 2 or 3</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"138\" width=\"376\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"24.0\" y=\"164.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Canada goose</text>\n<text x=\"376.0\" y=\"164.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"end\">Steel BB</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"184\" width=\"376\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"24.0\" y=\"210.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ruffed grouse</text>\n<text x=\"376.0\" y=\"210.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4e4132\" text-anchor=\"end\">Lead No. 7.5 or 6</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"230\" width=\"376\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"24.0\" y=\"256.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Older gun</text>\n<text x=\"376.0\" y=\"256.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"end\">Bismuth (ask the maker)</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"290.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Starting points (Tip). Pattern to be sure.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ducks: steel No. 2 or 3. Geese: steel BB. Grouse: lead No. 7.5 or 6 (Tip, 65 to 70%).</li><li>Pattern your pick before the hunt (<a href=\"#/s/mc-shotgun-06\">Chapter 6</a>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the picks in full</summary><ul><li>Ducks and geese: <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide\">Ammo for your guns</a> picks steel No. 2 or 3 for ducks, No. 4 for teal, BB for geese <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Grouse: 28 to 32 g (1 to 1 1/8 oz) of lead No. 7.5 or 6 (60%, <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09/4\">Grouse Masterclass</a>).</li><li>Duck and grouse on the same day: carry only steel. Steel No. 6 works on grouse (Tip). A lead grouse shell in your vest on a duck hunt breaks s. 38(1) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Ranges: ducks inside 35 m (38 yd), grouse inside about 25 m (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-skills/5\">Shotgun skills</a>).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Empty every pocket before the marsh. The officer counts what is in your coat, not what is in your gun.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>A forgotten lead grouse shell in a duck coat.</li><li>Full choke and big steel in a gun not rated for it.</li><li>Buying the most expensive shell instead of patterning a cheap one.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Two shell bags: orange for upland lead, green for steel. Only the green one goes in the boat.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Federal and BC law read directly <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Densities and sizes from secondary sources (65 to 70%). Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2022-105/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022</a>, s. 37 and 38, via the app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 13 (lead ban notice) and page 27 (Delta and Surrey dykes), via the app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shot_(pellet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikipedia: shot (pellet)</a>): steel hardness, bismuth in older guns. Read 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.nwtf.org/content-hub/turkey-load-pellet-science\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NWTF: turkey load pellet science</a> and <a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/guns/tungsten-super-shot-deadliest-bird-shot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life: tungsten super shot</a>: densities, search previews 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://berettaweb.com/Munuals/Beretta%20Owner%20Manual%20A300%20Outlander%20LD.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Beretta A300 Outlander instruction manual, 09/2011</a>: HP cartridge caution, factory ammunition. Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>Shell picks: <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide\">Ammo for your guns</a> and <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09\">Grouse Masterclass</a> (60 to 70%)</li></ul></details>"]